{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785443136,"nonce":"yUNVEOtply/0sdL2n/NxI+XdKcQ=","title":"ADR-0064 s1 follow-up: the re-ingest flush reads and re-hashes every blob before asking cold whether it needs it","message":"Found by review of the slice that landed `flush_to_cold` (`crates/scarab-server/src/workspaced.rs`).\n\n`flush_set_of` walks the whole snapshot, so the flush reads every blob out of warm — and `S3Storage::get_blob` re-verifies SHA-256 over every byte (`crates/scarab-storage-s3/src/lib.rs:938-943`) — and only then HEADs cold via `put_if_absent`. On a 50k-file workspace that is 50k full reads plus 50k re-hashes per Step boundary, where `ingest_with_baseline`'s `Verdict::Reuse` previously read nothing at all.\n\nThat is the per-file cost ADR-0061 measured at 81-88% of the drain, reintroduced on the archival leg. The slice traded it deliberately for correctness — a flush that skips reused blobs publishes a cold tree with absent children once cold's GC has swept the parent, because cold's GC deletes from cold only while warm has no eviction implemented at all.\n\n**The fix is to ask cold what it is missing BEFORE reading anything out of warm**, and read only the misses.\n\nBlocked on a public existence primitive. `S3Storage::put_if_absent` and `store_addressed` are private to `scarab-storage-s3`; `ObjectStore::get` downloads the body; `list_objects` would list the whole `blobs/` prefix. What is wanted is roughly `pub async fn has(\u0026self, key: \u0026str) -\u003e Result\u003cbool, StorageError\u003e` on `S3Storage`, plus a `buffer_unordered` probe pass in `flush_to_cold`.\n\n**Do NOT solve this by adding a method to the `Cas` trait**, and especially not one with a defaulted body: a default returning \"nothing missing\" is indistinguishable from the legitimate case and is the silent-skip shape this repo has already been bitten by. `flush_to_cold`'s cold parameter is already the concrete `\u0026S3Storage` so that the fix stays on the concrete type.\n\n- [ ] Cold is probed for the inventory before any warm read\n- [ ] Only the misses are read and uploaded\n- [ ] No `Cas` trait change; no defaulted method\n- [ ] A test that a flush whose inventory cold already holds performs zero warm blob reads","files":null}]}